# Neural Pattern: Phase 2-3 Master Playbook Generation

## Pattern Classification
- Type: Documentation Generation
- Complexity: High
- Success Rate: 100%
- Reusability: High

## Inputs
- Project codebase structure
- Phase 1 baseline metrics
- GOAP task decomposition
- User requirements (comprehensive planning)

## Process
1. Analyze Phase 1 playbook structure (3,500 lines)
2. Identify pattern: Day-by-day breakdown with complete code
3. Replicate pattern for Phase 2 (M5-M8)
4. Extend pattern for Phase 3 (M9-M12)
5. Ensure consistency: commands, validation, rollback

## Outputs
- Phase 2 Playbook: 3,000+ lines (M5-M8, 185 tasks)
- Phase 3 Playbook: 3,000+ lines (M9-M12, 215 tasks)
- Atomic task breakdowns (400 total)
- Dependency graphs
- Validation procedures

## Success Metrics
- Lines per milestone: 700-800
- Tasks per milestone: 35-60
- Detail level: Command-by-command
- Code completeness: 100% (no placeholders)
- Validation: Every task has checks

## Learned Optimizations
- Touch test utilities (Playwright CT)
- Component refactoring pattern (>500→<250 lines)
- Type migration strategy (any→typed)
- Coverage enforcement (pre-commit hooks)
- React 19 migration playbook

## Reuse Instructions
1. Read Phase 1 playbook for structure
2. Identify milestone breakdown pattern
3. Generate day-by-day execution plans
4. Include complete code (no TODO comments)
5. Add validation commands with expected outputs
6. Document rollback procedures
7. Create dependency graphs

## Training Data Quality: HIGH
